IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 1260 of 2022
CITATION: (2023) 1 SCC 578
YEAR: 2022

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, Hima Kohli

PARTIES:
Dashrathbhai Patel vs Hitesh Patel

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 138 NI Act, Section 56 NI Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
part payment, endorsement of payment, actual debt due

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that where part-payment has been made before presentation, failure to endorse part-payment on cheque under Section 56 prevents Section 138 from being triggered for original full amount.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 138 NI Act, Section 56 NI Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

